# SYSGEN - Install or export a boot system

```text
SYSGEN source: destination:
SYSGEN package destination:
```

## Install a system

Prepare the destination disk with the correct format for the target
machine. Write a matching system package to its reserved tracks. The
ordinary startup files still need to be on the disk.

```text
SYSGEN A:SYSTEM.SYS D:
```

Check the target drive before confirming. Use [DUP](DUP.HLP) when you
want a complete disk copy.

## Export an installed system

```text
SYSGEN A: D:SAVED.SYS
```

Read the installed system tracks on A and save them as a package on D.
With no arguments, SYSGEN guides you through source and destination
selection.
